  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Closed stabilizers and density",
  "statement": "Let $S\\subseteq V$ be a vector subspace. The stabilizer\n$\\operatorname{Stab}_{\\operatorname{GL}(V)}(S)$ is Zariski closed.\nConsequently $S$ is $\\Pi$-stable if and only if it is\n$H_{\\mathrm{geom}}$-stable.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-algebraic-groups-lie-algebras/sk-i-restriction/lem-wf-stabilizer-density.md",
    "place": "node lem-wf-stabilizer-density, order 2515"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Choose a basis whose first vectors span $S$. The condition that a\nmatrix preserve $S$ says that each lower-left matrix entry is zero,\nwhich is a finite list of polynomial equations. The stabilizer is\ntherefore closed. If $S$ is $\\Pi$-stable, this closed stabilizer\ncontains $\\rho(\\Pi)$, hence contains its Zariski closure by\n[def-wf-geometric-monodromy-group]; the converse is immediate.",
      "uses": [
        "def-wf-geometric-monodromy-group"
      ],
      "elementary": false
    }
  ],
